                          "Comments": "Clay - ",
                          "Name": "Grey Vertosol NMM",
                          "ResourceName": null,
                          "Children": [
                            {
                              "$type": "Models.Memo, Models",
                              "Text": "If you look at the weather files all experiments were pre irrigated in late September – early October so soil profile would have been at DUL below surface layer(s) at planting. \n\nA combination of post establishment rain, clay soil and very slow crop growth (cold soil and temperatures) meant probes to 1.3 m could not be installed until about a month after establishment. \n\nOnly the surface layers would have dried slightly by 1st probe readings. \n\nThe plants are tiny at this stage at Narrabri so you could assume Dul below about 15 cm. \n\nAPSIM could calculate the soil Et between planting and  probe measurement. Then if needed re set soil water = observed at first measurement and let simulation continue from that point – the error should be small.",
                              "Name": "Memo",
                              "ResourceName": null,
                              "Children": [],
                              "Enabled": true,
                              "ReadOnly": false
                            },
